{
  "openapi": "3.0.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "IdentyClaw Federated Peer API (RODiT)",
    "version": "2025.10.01",
    "description": "# IdentyClaw federated peer API\n\nReusable pattern for **federated API authentication**: IdentyClaw **Passport** holders prove possession of their keys against **this peer**, receive a **peer-minted JWT**, and call protected routes. Built on `@rodit/rodit-auth-be` 9.x.\n\nCRUDA (`/api/cruda/*`) is only a sample protected resource — replace it with your domain.\n\n## Federation model\n\n| Identity surface | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| **IdentyClaw home** (`https://api.identyclaw.com`) | Passport / HOLA enrollment. Home JWT does **not** authorize this peer's protected routes. |\n| **This peer** (your `apiEndpoint`) | Own RODiT service credentials. Mint JWTs via `POST /api/login`. Clients must login **against this base URL**. |\n\nEach federated peer is an independent auth boundary. Agents and apps remint a JWT per `apiEndpoint`. Do not reuse a token from another peer or from home.\n\n```\nPassport keys (Ed25519)\n        │\n        ▼\nGET /api/login/timestamp  →  challenge (timestamp + timestamp_iso)\n        │\n        ▼\nSign UTF-8: identifier + timestamp_iso  →  POST /api/login\n        │\n        ▼\nPeer JWT (Authorization: Bearer)  →  protected routes + METHOD_PERMISSION_MAP\n```\n\n## Authentication (raw)\n\n1. `GET /api/login/timestamp` — challenge pair from this peer.\n2. Sign UTF-8 `identifier + timestamp_iso` (Ed25519 → base64url). Identifier is Passport `roditid` (12 letters) or NEAR `accountid` (64-hex).\n3. `POST /api/login` — send signature + exactly one of `timestamp` / `timestamp_iso`.\n4. Call protected routes with `Authorization: Bearer <jwt_token>` (body field is `jwt_token`, not `token`).\n5. `POST /api/logout` — invalidate session (`authenticateForLogout` allows expired JWTs with valid signature).\n\n## OpenClaw / agents\n\nPreferred: `identyclaw_ensure_session({ apiEndpoint })` then `identyclaw_request({ method, path, apiEndpoint })`. The plugin caches the peer JWT and never returns it to the model.\n\nDiscovery: `GET /`, `GET /.well-known/mcp`, `GET /api/mcp/resource/doc:skills`.\n\n## Authorization\n\nProtected showcase routes under `/api/cruda/*` require both:\n\n1. Valid peer JWT (`authenticate`)\n2. Verb allowed by `METHOD_PERMISSION_MAP` (`authorize`) — keys such as `create`, `list`, `read`, `update`, `destroy`\n\nSessions admin and signclient follow the same RODiT permission patterns. See config `METHOD_PERMISSION_MAP`.\n\n## Errors\n\n`{ error: { code, message, details? }, requestId, timestamp }` — see `components.schemas.ErrorResponse`.\n\n## Scaffold usage\n\n1. Keep auth, discovery, health, swagger, and permission-map wiring.\n2. Replace or extend `/api/cruda` with your resources; mount with authenticate + authorize.\n3. Point `SERVICE_NAME` / nginx / OpenAPI `servers` at your peer hostname.\n4. Publish this OpenAPI as the contract for Passport holders integrating with your peer.\n",
    "termsOfService": "https://identyclaw.com",
    "contact": {
      "name": "Discernible Inc.",
      "url": "https://identyclaw.com",
      "email": "support@rodit-tech.com"
